# .privacy-deny.example — example personal-identity deny-list for privacy-scan.mjs
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file:   cp scripts/.privacy-deny.example scripts/.privacy-deny.local
#   2. Add your real personal terms to scripts/.privacy-deny.local
#   3. Run:              node scripts/privacy-scan.mjs
#
# The .local copy is git-ignored, so your personal terms are NEVER committed.
# This .example file is committed and must contain ONLY placeholders + comments.
#
# FORMAT
#   - One JavaScript RegExp (source only — no surrounding slashes) per line.
#   - Lines starting with '#' are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
#   - Patterns are matched against each line of every scanned text file.
#   - Use word boundaries (\b) to avoid matching inside larger words.
#   - Use (?i) is NOT supported; matching is case-sensitive. Add variants if needed.
#
# EXAMPLES (replace the placeholders below — do not commit real values here)

# Your name and common variants:
# \bYourFirstName\b
# \bYourFirstName\s+YourLastName\b

# Nicknames or family names that should never ship publicly:
# \bYourNickname\b

# Personal domains / project codenames:
# yourdomain\.com
# YourPrivateProjectName

# Social handles:
# @your_handle

# Anything else you want kept out of the public repo:
# \bYourCompanyInternalName\b
